# tools/r/rune_assert_sweep.rish -- assert coverage, proven across the rooms rather than a list.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/r/rune_assert_sweep.rish
#
# WHY THIS RUNG. TAME root rule 2 asks every function to state its invariants -- an `assert` at
# construction, mutation and postcondition, each preceded by a `// invariant:` comment. This is the
# tool `context/TAME_CORE.md` names for that rule, so what it reads is what the rule is held to.
#
# WHAT CHANGED, and why it needed changing. From `20260810` until `20260908` this rung read twelve
# file paths typed into the line below -- 1.1 percent of the 1,127 authored `.rye` the TAME rooms
# hold. TAME_CORE named it the third of three guards reading a hand-typed list, after
# `opening_lines` and `tame_check` widened the same week, and called that "the argument for widening
# the third." The reading is now derived from `tools/fixtures/t/tame_style_rooms.txt`, the roster
# five readers now share.
#
# WHAT THE WIDENING FOUND, and it is a boundary rather than a count. The elder twelve are NOT a
# subset of the roster: five of them sit in four rooms the roster does not name at all --
# `mandate/`, `kumara/`, `settlement/` and `sundial/`. Deriving alone would have dropped five gated
# files while the printed population grew a hundredfold, which is a guard reading more and proving
# less. So the twelve keep a leg of their own, read by name whatever the roster holds.
#
# WHAT THE THIRD READING FOUND, added `20260908.170042`, and it is the word EACH. Both readings
# below are FILE questions -- does this file assert at all, does it name an invariant anywhere --
# and the rule they serve asks that each assert be preceded by its own `// invariant:` comment. The
# scan's own header had claimed to count that from the day it was written. Measured across the same
# rooms: 24,495 asserts stand in the 859 asserting module sources and **6,619 name nothing**, so
# 73 percent of ASSERTS are named, while 899 of the 1,100 function-bearing files -- 82 percent --
# already satisfied the file reading beside it. The elder reading is a strict subset of the new one,
# proven by plant rather than argued.
#
# AND THE SPLIT IS WHAT KEEPS IT HONEST. A `*_witness.rye` asserts about another program's OUTPUT,
# so 2,588 unnamed asserts there are correct practice rather than debt; they are reported and gated
# nowhere. Read whole, `glow/` scores 1.1 percent named and looks like the worst room in the tree;
# read on its modules alone it scores 92 percent, and the 2,331 asserts were its witnesses all
# along.
#
# WHAT IS PROVEN, on metal.
#   The twelve elder cores keep their asserts, each printed by name, at a ceiling of zero.
#   Across 1,127 authored sources in the twenty rooms: 1,100 carry functions, 100 of those carry no
#   `assert(` at all, and 101 more assert without naming a single `// invariant:`.
#   Across the 859 asserting module sources among them: 6,619 of 24,495 asserts name no invariant.
#
# WHAT IS RATCHETED rather than gated, and why. All three derived readings are ceilings that only
# fall. A wall at zero would ask for two hundred files, or six thousand comments, to be repaired in
# one lap, and a wall that reds on honest work is a wall somebody turns off. Each of those comments
# has to state a true reason rather than restate the line beneath it, so this is a ratchet on
# purpose and not merely by scale. TAME's own gate-versus-ratchet split says the same: migrate on
# touch.
#
# WHAT IS NOT PROVEN. That an assert is the RIGHT assert, that a named `// invariant:` states a true
# one, or that a bound is ever checked. This counts whether a file speaks at all.

say "rune-assert-sweep: Language EN -- assert coverage, read across the rooms."
say "rune-assert-sweep: Style Gauge, Meter -- the count is the sentence."
say "rune-assert-sweep: Lens TAME -- a guard reads the population, never a list of it."

let result = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/r/rune_assert_sweep_scan.sh"]
assert result.ok else "rune-assert-sweep: the scan failed -- read the rooms file it was handed"

say result.out

assert result.out contains "elder_faults=0 ceiling=0" else "rune-assert-sweep RED: a gated core dropped to zero asserts"
assert result.out contains "elder_roster=12" else "rune-assert-sweep RED: the elder roster lost a file"
assert result.out contains "ratchets_over_ceiling=0" else "rune-assert-sweep RED: an assert ratchet rose past its ceiling -- ceilings only fall"
assert result.out contains "module_assert=" else "rune-assert-sweep: the per-assert reading must be printed, not merely computed"
assert result.out contains "proving_assert=" else "rune-assert-sweep: the proving half is reported even though it gates nothing"
assert result.out contains "verdict=read" else "rune-assert-sweep: the scan must finish before it is believed"

# THE CONTROL, on every run rather than on a hand's memory. Each reading above is a claim about
# files nobody typed, so each is planted in a throwaway pen, counted while it stands, and read back
# to zero once it is lifted. Both ratchets are shown from the failing side, which the pen's own
# ceiling of zero is what buys.
let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/r/rune_assert_control.sh"]
assert control.ok else "rune-assert-sweep: the control must complete"
say control.out
assert control.out contains "clean_counted=yes" else "rune-assert-sweep: an authored .rye must be counted"
assert control.out contains "clean_reads_zero=yes" else "rune-assert-sweep: a file that states its invariant must read zero rather than merely pass"
assert control.out contains "roster_comment_stripped=yes" else "rune-assert-sweep: a commented roster line must name no room"
assert control.out contains "zero_assert_counted=yes" else "rune-assert-sweep: a function-bearing file with no assert must be counted"
assert control.out contains "zero_assert_leaves_gap_alone=yes" else "rune-assert-sweep: the two ratchets must move apart"
assert control.out contains "zero_assert_over_ceiling_refused=yes" else "rune-assert-sweep: the zero-assert ceiling must refuse from the failing side"
assert control.out contains "zero_assert_named=yes" else "rune-assert-sweep: a ratchet over its ceiling must name the file"
assert control.out contains "zero_assert_cleared=yes" else "rune-assert-sweep: the count must fall back to zero once the plant is lifted"
assert control.out contains "invariant_gap_counted=yes" else "rune-assert-sweep: an assert naming no // invariant: must be counted"
assert control.out contains "invariant_gap_leaves_zero_alone=yes" else "rune-assert-sweep: the invariant gap must leave the zero-assert count alone"
assert control.out contains "invariant_gap_over_ceiling_refused=yes" else "rune-assert-sweep: the invariant-gap ceiling must refuse from the failing side"
assert control.out contains "invariant_gap_cleared=yes" else "rune-assert-sweep: the gap must clear once the comment arrives"
assert control.out contains "clean_assert_named=yes" else "rune-assert-sweep: an assert under its own comment must read named"
assert control.out contains "unnamed_assert_counted=yes" else "rune-assert-sweep: an assert naming nothing must be counted inside a file that names one"
assert control.out contains "module_asserts_counted=yes" else "rune-assert-sweep: the denominator must count every module assert"
assert control.out contains "unnamed_leaves_gap_alone=yes" else "rune-assert-sweep: the per-assert reading must move without the file reading"
assert control.out contains "unnamed_assert_named=yes" else "rune-assert-sweep: a red must name the file and its count"
assert control.out contains "unnamed_over_ceiling_refused=yes" else "rune-assert-sweep: the per-assert ceiling must refuse from the failing side"
assert control.out contains "run_under_one_comment_named=yes" else "rune-assert-sweep: a run of asserts under one comment is named"
assert control.out contains "comment_block_names=yes" else "rune-assert-sweep: a comment block opening on the invariant names what follows"
assert control.out contains "unnamed_assert_cleared=yes" else "rune-assert-sweep: the count must fall back once the plant is lifted"
assert control.out contains "proving_counted_apart=yes" else "rune-assert-sweep: a witness assert lands in the proving half"
assert control.out contains "proving_leaves_module_alone=yes" else "rune-assert-sweep: a witness assert must not enter the gated reading"
assert control.out contains "proving_gates_nothing=yes" else "rune-assert-sweep: the proving half gates nothing"
assert control.out contains "same_bytes_module_counted=yes" else "rune-assert-sweep: the same bytes under a module name must be counted"
assert control.out contains "no_fn_not_fn_bearing=yes" else "rune-assert-sweep: a file declaring no fn states no invariant and is asked for none"
assert control.out contains "qualified_counts_as_assert=yes" else "rune-assert-sweep: a qualified std.debug.assert( still states an invariant"
assert control.out contains "near_miss_not_an_assert=yes" else "rune-assert-sweep: an identifier ending in assert is a different function"
assert control.out contains "symlink_and_bin_skipped=yes" else "rune-assert-sweep: a symlink and a bin/ path stay outside the population"
assert control.out contains "pen_elder_absent=yes" else "rune-assert-sweep: a pen owns no tree paths, so the elder leg reports absent"
assert control.out contains "tree_elder_roster_twelve=yes" else "rune-assert-sweep: the elder roster must still read twelve"
assert control.out contains "absent_roster_refused=yes" else "rune-assert-sweep: an absent rooms file must refuse rather than read an empty population"
assert control.out contains "control=done" else "rune-assert-sweep: the control must run to its end"

say "GREEN: rune-assert-sweep -- twelve cores keep their asserts; the three ratchets hold under their ceilings"
